            "name": "Section 5.2 Exclusion Criteria",
            "summary": "Exclusion Criterion #16: removed \"Exception: Short-term treatment with insulin for <14 days is allowed for certain clinical situations, such as, elective surgery, during hospitalization, hyperosmolar states, or acute illness.\"\nEdited Exclusion Criterion #36 to remove \", except for the use of insulin for treatment of gestational diabetes or acute, temporary use of insulin (≤14 days), for example, for acute illness, hospitalization, elective surgery.\"\nEdited Exclusion Criterion #40 to add \"Note: Insulin therapy is not allowed within 90 days prior to Visit 1.\"",
